1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,620
What if your dentist could tell you more
about your health

2
00:00:02,620 --> 00:00:03,300
than your teeth?

3
00:00:03,940 --> 00:00:05,260
Hi, I'm Dr. Dickson.

4
00:00:05,880 --> 00:00:07,280
Let me ask you a question.

5
00:00:07,940 --> 00:00:09,760
When was the last time your dentist talked
to you

6
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:10,360
about your sleep?

7
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:11,500
Or inflammation?

8
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:12,800
Or breathing?

9
00:00:13,540 --> 00:00:17,100
Or how your oral health might affect the
rest of your body?

10
00:00:17,340 --> 00:00:20,100
The Forma Method is a comprehensive health
evaluation

11
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:22,380
that uses your mouth as a window

12
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:24,520
into your overall health, sleep,

13
00:00:24,980 --> 00:00:26,240
inflammation, and longevity.

14
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:28,600
Instead of looking at one tooth at a time,

15
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:30,020
we look at the complete picture.

16
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:32,100
We ask, why is this happening?

17
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:33,460
What caused this?

18
00:00:33,740 --> 00:00:34,920
What can we learn from it?

19
00:00:35,140 --> 00:00:37,260
And how can we help prevent future problems?

20
00:00:37,740 --> 00:00:39,740
The goal is not simply healthier teeth.

21
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:41,460
The goal is a healthier you.

22
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:44,100
You want a dental office where you feel
comfortable.

23
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:45,920
You want a team that listens.

24
00:00:46,440 --> 00:00:48,160
You want recommendations you can trust.

25
00:00:48,740 --> 00:00:51,020
And you want to know that the people caring
for you

26
00:00:51,020 --> 00:00:53,000
genuinely have your best interest at heart.

27
00:00:53,860 --> 00:00:55,500
That's exactly the type of practice

28
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:56,660
we've worked hard to create.

29
00:00:56,660 --> 00:00:59,320
Phase one, we call this discover.

30
00:01:00,080 --> 00:01:01,780
This is where we gather information.

31
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:05,100
We use digital photography, intraoral
scanning,

32
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:08,180
facial scanning, CBCT imaging,

33
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:11,920
comprehensive health histories, and sleep
airway screening.

34
00:01:12,580 --> 00:01:14,800
This gives us an incredibly detailed
understanding

35
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:15,460
of your health.

36
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,460
Think of it like creating a blueprint.

37
00:01:17,860 --> 00:01:20,240
Before building a home, you need plans.

38
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:22,580
Before creating a personalized health
strategy,

39
00:01:22,820 --> 00:01:23,620
we need data.

40
00:01:24,380 --> 00:01:25,560
So why this matters?

41
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:29,060
Most people have never seen their oral
health this way.

42
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:31,340
Many patients are surprised when they learn

43
00:01:31,340 --> 00:01:33,680
their grinding may be related to airway
issues.

44
00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:36,500
Their worn teeth may be connected to sleep
problems.

45
00:01:37,332 --> 00:01:38,780
Their inflammation may be affecting

46
00:01:38,780 --> 00:01:39,960
more than just their gums.

47
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:42,240
Their jaw position may be contributing

48
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:44,000
to headaches or discomfort.

49
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:47,440
Their oral bacteria may be influencing
overall health.

50
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:49,720
The earlier we identify these issues,

51
00:01:49,980 --> 00:01:51,760
the more options we have to address them.

52
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:54,760
If your jaw is sore, tight, clicking,

53
00:01:54,760 --> 00:01:56,720
or just feels tired all the time,

54
00:01:57,040 --> 00:01:58,920
you might assume you have TMJ.

55
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:01,560
But TMJ is actually the name of the joint,

56
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:03,280
the temporomandibular joint.

57
00:02:03,660 --> 00:02:04,940
And there are several different things

58
00:02:04,940 --> 00:02:06,540
that can cause pain in this area.

59
00:02:07,020 --> 00:02:09,220
Many people clench their teeth throughout
the day

60
00:02:09,220 --> 00:02:10,880
without even realizing it.

61
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:13,260
Others may grind or clench while they're
sleeping.

62
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:15,140
That can overwork the muscles

63
00:02:15,140 --> 00:02:16,940
around the jaw and the temples.

64
00:02:17,360 --> 00:02:19,340
The important thing is that your jaw pain

65
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:21,980
isn't one diagnosis and the right treatment

66
00:02:21,980 --> 00:02:24,760
depends on identifying what's actually
causing it.

67
00:02:25,180 --> 00:02:26,580
If your jaw pain is persistent,

68
00:02:27,060 --> 00:02:27,900
your jaw's locking,

69
00:02:28,180 --> 00:02:30,280
or you're having difficulty opening
comfortably,

70
00:02:30,980 --> 00:02:32,920
that's a good reason to have it evaluated.

71
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:34,640
Phase two, understand.

72
00:02:35,440 --> 00:02:37,340
Data by itself doesn't improve health.

73
00:02:38,380 --> 00:02:38,820
Understanding does.

74
00:02:39,380 --> 00:02:40,540
After gathering information,

75
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:42,580
we review everything together.

76
00:02:42,940 --> 00:02:44,680
We show you exactly what we're seeing.

77
00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:47,660
We explain what's healthy, what's
concerning,

78
00:02:48,180 --> 00:02:50,780
what may need attention, and why it matters.

79
00:02:50,780 --> 00:02:53,360
Our patients often tell us this is the first
time

80
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:55,720
they've truly understood what's happening in
their mouth.

81
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:59,720
No confusing terminology, no pressure, just
clarity.

82
00:03:00,220 --> 00:03:02,160
Whether you're coming in for a routine
cleaning,

83
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:04,360
have concerns about your dental health,

84
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:06,520
or you're interested in improving your
smile,

85
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:08,100
our goal is always the same,

86
00:03:08,260 --> 00:03:10,420
to help you feel informed, comfortable,

87
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:12,300
and confident in your care.

88
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:14,820
Phase three, personalized health plan.

89
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:16,840
Every patient is different.

90
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:19,780
That's why every Forma Method plan is
customized.

91
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:22,880
Your plan may include preventative care,

92
00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:26,000
airway improvements, sleep evaluation,

93
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:30,680
bite optimization, gum therapy, smile
enhancement,

94
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:32,260
nutritional recommendations,

95
00:03:32,740 --> 00:03:34,220
and long-term health monitoring.

96
00:03:34,740 --> 00:03:35,760
The goal is simple.

97
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:39,100
Help you maintain your health, function,
appearance,

98
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:41,360
and quality of life for decades to come.

99
00:03:41,980 --> 00:03:43,200
The longevity connection.

100
00:03:44,180 --> 00:03:46,260
One of the reasons patients are so excited

101
00:03:46,260 --> 00:03:48,600
about the Forma Method is because it aligns

102
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:50,240
with a growing interest in longevity.

103
00:03:51,100 --> 00:03:52,380
People want more than treatment.

104
00:03:52,780 --> 00:03:53,680
They want prevention.

105
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:54,980
They want answers.

106
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:56,420
They want to age well.

107
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:59,980
The mouth provides valuable clues about
what's happening

108
00:03:59,980 --> 00:04:01,160
throughout the rest of the body.

109
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:03,360
By identifying concerns earlier,

110
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:06,300
we can often help patients make better
decisions

111
00:04:06,300 --> 00:04:08,360
before problems become larger.

112
00:04:08,720 --> 00:04:09,940
Our philosophy is simple.

113
00:04:10,460 --> 00:04:11,760
Treat every patient the way

114
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:13,400
we would want our own family treated.

115
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:16,140
That means taking the time to get to know
you,

116
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:17,520
understand your goals,

117
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:18,900
answer your questions,

118
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:21,900
and help you make confident decisions about
your health.

119
00:04:22,340 --> 00:04:24,560
We don't believe in rushing people through
appointments.

120
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:27,360
We don't believe in pressuring patients into
treatment.

121
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:29,680
We want you to feel welcomed, respected,

122
00:04:29,820 --> 00:04:31,500
and supported every step of the way.

123
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:34,440
I invite you to experience a Forma Method
for yourself.

124
00:04:35,180 --> 00:04:35,960
During your visit,

125
00:04:36,080 --> 00:04:38,320
we'll perform a comprehensive evaluation,

126
00:04:38,960 --> 00:04:40,380
review our findings together,

127
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:43,320
and help you better understand your health,

128
00:04:43,660 --> 00:04:45,900
your risks, and your opportunities for
improvement.

129
00:04:46,580 --> 00:04:48,000
Thank you for spending this time with me.

130
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:50,120
My team and I look forward to meeting you

131
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:51,820
and helping you discover what's possible

132
00:04:51,820 --> 00:04:52,880
through the Forma Method.

133
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:55,860
Schedule your Forma Method health evaluation
today.
